A standalone comment block directly above :PROCEDURE (no blank line
between) is attached: the separating blank line goes above the comment
block, not between it and the keyword. A comment already separated from
its :PROCEDURE by a blank line is not attached, and normalization applies
between that comment and the :PROCEDURE (fmt.blank_lines_between_procs).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE First;
:RETURN 1;
:ENDPROC;
/* Second: returns two;
/* used by the report header;
:PROCEDURE Second;
:RETURN 2;
:ENDPROC;
/* Loose note about Third;


:PROCEDURE Third;
:RETURN 3;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE First;
	:RETURN 1;
:ENDPROC;

/* Second: returns two;
/* used by the report header;
:PROCEDURE Second;
	:RETURN 2;
:ENDPROC;

/* Loose note about Third;

:PROCEDURE Third;
	:RETURN 3;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
